Q: Can I put frozen chicken straight into the slow cooker? 
A: No, it's not recommended to put frozen chicken directly into the slow cooker. The cold temperature can cause the meat to become tough and dry over time. It's best to thaw the chicken in the refrigerator overnight or for at least 8 hours before cooking it in the slow cooker. This will help soften the meat and make it more tender.
